## What must have a test

- **Any change to tajweed rules or colours** — add or update assertions in
  `tajweed_baqarah_test.dart`, verified against quran.com's `uthmani_tajweed` API.
  Never change an expected colour without a source to justify it. Use `/verify-tajweed`.
- **Any new or changed `AppRoute`** — add a case to `router_paths_test.dart`.
- **Any change to `ArabicText`, font handling, or reader text styling** — the goldens
  in `arabic_rendering_test.dart` must be regenerated and visually reviewed.

## Loading fixtures

Load asset fixtures with `dart:io` `File`, not `rootBundle`:

```dart
final raw = await File('assets/quran/ar/2.json').readAsString();
```

Paths are relative to the package root, which is the working directory under
`flutter test`. `rootBundle` requires an asset bundle that plain unit tests don't have.

## Arabic text in tests

- **Load real fonts before rendering Arabic.** Without a `FontLoader`, the test
  framework substitutes a fallback font and Arabic renders as boxes, so any layout
  or golden assertion is meaningless. See `_loadArabicFonts()` in
  `arabic_rendering_test.dart`.
- **Never strip diacritics to make an assertion pass.** Assert on the exact string.
- Prefer asserting on `tajweedColorAssignments(text)` (no `BuildContext` needed) over
  driving `tajweedSpans()` through a widget when you only care about colours.

## Golden tests

- Tag them `golden` (declared in `dart_test.yaml`) so CI can exclude them. Font
  rasterization differs across platforms, so goldens generated on Windows will not
  match a Linux CI runner. They are a **local** regression check.
- Regenerate with `flutter test --update-goldens`, then **open the PNG and look at it**.
  A golden is only as good as the first human review — clipped diacritics and wrong
  tajweed colours both look like "just a diff" otherwise.
- Keep goldens narrow: fix the widget size, theme, font, and zoom explicitly so a
  diff means a real rendering change and not an unrelated theme tweak.

## Pumping a page that loads assets

Two session caches will make the **second** test in a file hang on its loading
spinner with no error to explain why. Each test runs in its own fake-async zone,
and a `Future` completed in a previous zone never delivers in the next:

```dart
setUp(() {
  QuranChaptersRepository.resetCache();  // also QuranArabicRepository,
  rootBundle.clear();                    // WordByWordRepository
});
```

`rootBundle` is the one that actually bites — it caches asset strings
independently of our repositories, so clearing only the repository is not
enough. Repositories that cache expose `@visibleForTesting resetCache()`; add
one when you introduce a new cache.

Do not try to diagnose this by pumping longer. Assert
`find.byType(CircularProgressIndicator)` is absent to fail fast with a clear
signal instead. Note that `pumpAndSettle` **cannot** be used while a progress
indicator is on screen, since it animates forever — pump a fixed number of
frames instead.

## Widget test conventions

- Wrap in `MaterialApp` with the real `buildLightTheme()` / `buildDarkTheme()` so tests
  catch theme regressions too.
- Pass `fontOverride:` and `tajweed:` explicitly to `ArabicText` rather than relying on
  `SettingsScope`, so the test is deterministic.
- Assert `tester.takeException()` is `null` after pumping — this is what catches
  `RenderFlex` overflow and layout assertions.
